=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7 feature surfaces do. The
  generated prompt's idealized "AutomationCard.xaml + AutomationCardViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/
  Automations" is mapped onto these real conventions: AutomationCard.Model.cs + AutomationCard.cs.
- The web AutomationCard is a PURELY PRESENTATIONAL card (it takes an `automation` prop + the `isFiring` /
  `vehicleName` flags and raises onToggle/onReEnable/onDelete/onTestRun callbacks); it NEVER fetches. The
  manifest therefore declares NO API data sources and a single `success` data state — there is no fetch-driven
  loading/empty/error branch to reproduce (ADR-006). The native surface mirrors this exactly: it is a
  ContentControl bound to an AutomationCardModel, all branch selection/label resolution/formatting happen in the
  WinUI-free AutomationCardProjection, and the host page (the automations list) wires the action events — the
  native analogue of the web callbacks. Web route is `(unrouted)` (the card is embedded by the automations list,
  not a navigable route), so no NavigationView entry is registered; the surface exposes a stable diagnostics slug
  (AutomationCardRegistration.Slug = "AutomationCard").
- Panel (ADR-005): the web <GlassPanel> maps to a tokenized TsGlassPanel (Mica/Acrylic glass) built in
  AutomationCard.cs#Render; firing automations gain the cyan accent glow (Glow=Cyan) and auto-disabled
  automations the danger accent border — the native analogue of the web ring/border. Every region inside (header
  row with the truncating name + status TsBadge + pulsing firing chip + pin/toggle/kebab cluster, the description
  line, the scoped-vehicle/all-vehicles chip row, the last-run/never-run + runs + fails + next-fire stats row, the
  auto-disabled reason banner and the warning/info conflict rows) is reproduced with Fluent controls + design
  tokens. No hardcoded colors/typography.
- i18n (ADR-014): every visible literal resolves through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names. All 19
  manifest keys are present in Strings/en/Resources.resw (verified: translation.automations.* + translation.
  common.cancel — MISSING_COUNT=0); the projection feeds the exact translation.* catalog keys and the web English
  default as the fallback, proven by the ReswLocalizer test. The ar/he catalogs lag en by design (translations
  land later); ILocalizer falls back to the English default until translated.
- a11y (ADR-015): decorative FontIcon glyphs are AccessibilityView.Raw (hidden from Narrator); every interactive
  element (pin, toggle, kebab, each menu item, delete dialog) carries an accessible name; the card composes a
  single meaningful Narrator name (name + status + vehicle + stats + reason + conflicts) via BuildAutomationName.
  Segoe Fluent glyphs stand in for the web Lucide icons.
- SI units (ADR): N/A — the card renders no unit-bearing physical quantity. Counts format through invariant
  ToString; the bespoke web `timeAgo` tiers (just now / Nm / Nh / Nd ago, Math.floor semantics) and the
  `formatDateTime` next-fire stamp are ported 1:1 through AutomationCardProjection / DateTimeFormatting at the
  display boundary.
- The implementation (AutomationCard.Model.cs 609 L + AutomationCard.cs 660 L) and its headless suite
  (AutomationCardTests.cs, 52 methods / 60 cases) were already committed by the feature-views surface phase
  (59fbf0a31). This W7 page gate verifies full manifest coverage (21/21), runs the windows triad + placeholder
  gate green, and records the parity ledger row + this evidence log. No red shipped; no stubs/placeholders.

